-- title:
--   Archimedean Euler identity for M and its cyclotomic dual
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $S$ be a finite set of rational primes, and let $M$ be a representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})=\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}\simeq_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$ on a finite-dimensional $\mathbb{Z}/p$-vector space. The set $S$ enters only through the index type $\mathrm{Unit}\oplus S$ of local places, and the place singled out here is the archimedean one $\mathrm{Sum.inl}\ ()$: the homomorphism `extArithLoc S (Sum.inl ())` is the inclusion `archimedeanLoc` of the subgroup `archimedeanDecomposition` of the absolute Galois group, so all cohomology below is that of this subgroup acting on the restriction of a global representation. Write $M^\vee(\chi)$ for `M.dualTwist (cycloChar p)`, the $\mathbb{Z}/p$-dual representation of $M$ multiplied by the mod $p$ cyclotomic character $\chi$, the character sending $\sigma$ to its action on $p$-th roots of unity, valued in $(\mathbb{Z}/p)^\times$. The assertion is the equality of $\mathbb{Z}/p$-dimensions
--   $$\dim (M)^{\mathrm{arch}} + \dim (M^\vee(\chi))^{\mathrm{arch}} + \dim H^1(\mathrm{arch}, M) = \dim M + 2\dim H^2_{\mathrm{cont}}(\mathrm{arch}, M),$$
--   where the first two terms are dimensions of invariants of the restricted representations, $H^1$ is the first group cohomology of the restriction, and $H^2_{\mathrm{cont}}$ is `continuousH2`, the quotient of the subgroup `levelCocycles₂` of $2$-cochains by the pullback of `levelCoboundaries₂` along its inclusion.
--
--   This is the archimedean contribution to the Greenberg–Wiles formula for the $\mathbb{Z}/p$-dimension of a Selmer group: the local factor at the real place, expressed as a relation between the invariants of $M$, those of its cyclotomic dual, and the higher cohomology of the decomposition group generated by complex conjugation. It is used by [`groupCohomology.greenbergWiles_eq_unramifiedMenu_extArithLoc`](thm.html#groupCohomology.greenbergWiles_eq_unramifiedMenu_extArithLoc), where the local terms over the places indexed by $\mathrm{Unit}\oplus S$ are assembled; its only arithmetic input is the value $-1$ of the mod $p$ cyclotomic character on complex conjugation, recorded in [`ExtCitation.cycloChar_complexConjugation_eq_neg_one`](thm.html#ExtCitation.cycloChar_complexConjugation_eq_neg_one).
-- source:
